So the number of trees depends on the initial condition and is not an easily reproducible property. I think those structures are pretty. And if you study them in more detail, you can show that there are fractal patterns. A fractal pattern means the pattern has a fractal dimension. So let me explain that a little bit. If you have a two-dimensional sheet, and you pick a point at random, and then you draw a circle with radius r around that point, that point, and you ask how many other points, how many other points on the sheet are on the sheet? How many other points are at distance r? So number of points on the sheet at distance r is proportional to r because it is a length of the circumference of a sphere. On the other hand, if you have a one-dimensional sheet, like a line, and do the same thing, pick a point and then draw a circle, you find only two points at distance r, no matter how big the radius is. So if you do the following plot, if we plot here, the number of points at distance r. And here we plot the radius. This is 2. So for a one-dimensional object, d is equal to 1. This is a constant. For a two object this is proportional to r. For a three object this is proportional to r squared. So the number of points of distance r is proportional to r to the power of d where d is a dimension. And this is a way to define a fractal dimension. You can even define negative dimensional objects with that.

Now, in an object like this, if you pick a point at random and draw a circle, the number of points at distance r does not grow, is not proportional to r. It is a power law, but it has a different proportionality. And so, if you study this object, you will find that the fractal dimension of the object is about 1.8. So, another way to look at this is a linear object, a one-dimensional object, every point has two neighbors. In a two-dimensional object, every point on a rectangular grid has four neighbors. But here, in this object, we have sometimes three neighbors, we have sometimes two neighbors. So it is not really a one-dimensional object, but it is also not a two-dimensional object. So it has a dimension between one and two. And so this is another reproducible property of the system. Actually I can show you some plots here. See this is the number of endpoints as a function of the number of particles. This illustrates that you have 22 percent endpoints. But this shows the number of particles within a certain radius r as a... And it shows that this goes like a power law. And therefore, the object has a reproducible fractal dimension. And this is a fractal dimension of the endpoints, which is two. So this means that the endpoints are homogeneously distributed, whereas the points which makes a connection to the grounded electrode are a fractal. So you can make the following interpretation of the structure. In this structure, the endpoints are homogeneously distributed and the rest of the ball bearings make sure those connections to the grounded electrode. So try to connect all the endpoints and they form a fractal network. But the endpoints themselves are homogeneously distributed.

