Q: They teach themselves I think by observing the world like nobody taught us how physics work. We taught it ourselves. But we observe. So those systems, you can show that systems when do, Hebbian learning can make abstractions, they can have frustrations, but they can make abstractions. You say, can detect correlations automatically. They do this automatically. So nobody taught us physics. We discovered physics just from observing the world. And those systems will have to do the same thing. They are not taught.

A: Does this mean there have to be more than the way it is supposed to be inspired? See, we are very limited. We can only memorize six or seven things at a time. Computers can memorize many more things at a time. So computers can detect correlations which are very hard for us to detect. If you open a physics textbook, it has never more than seven variables in it, because we cannot memorize more than seven variables. A computer can deal with concepts which are much more abstract than what we can do. And so we are sort of severely limited by our hardware. And so I think those systems can easily do what we do and more.

